      "problem": "If $-22+x=11$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the left-hand side so that the first term contains the variable.\n\n$$\nx-22=11\n$$\n\nTo isolate $x$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $22$ from $x$, which is *adding* $22$ to $x.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-22 & =11 \\\\ x-22+22 & =11+22 \\\\ x+0 & =33 \\\\ x & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$",
